==In animation==
[[File:Rosebay.png|thumb|250px|Rosebay, a Pokémornithologist in {{aniseries|DP}}]]
Several Bird Keepers appear in [[Johto]]: [[Malachi]] and [[Denjirō]] in ''[[EP164|Carrying On!]]'', [[Wilbur]] in ''[[EP211|Fly Me to the Moon]]'', [[Wings Alexander]] in ''[[EP223|Throwing in the Noctowl]]''.

In {{aniseries|DP}}, [[Rosebay]], the [[character of the day]] of ''[[DP013|A Staravia is Born!]]'', appears to be a female Bird Keeper and refers to herself as a Pokémornithologist. This character being a female is consistent with the depiction of the Bird Keepers in {{3v2|Diamond|Pearl|Platinum}}.
{{-}}

==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
===={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}====
[[File:Bird Keeper Adventures.png|thumb|left|200px|A male Bird Keeper in Pokémon Adventures]]
A male Bird Keeper first appeared in ''[[PS092|Who Gives a Hoothoot?]]'', where he hosted a game in which the participant has to capture the {{p|Wooper}} that are let loose in a given amount of time. So far, none of the challengers have succeeded. {{adv|Gold}} accepts the Bird Keeper's challenge, much to his amusement. Unbeknownst to the Bird Keeper, Gold had his {{p|Aipom}}, [[Aibo]], use {{m|Swagger}} to confuse Hoothoot before they began. The Bird Keeper started the challenge, and Gold captured many Wooper. When the Bird Keeper was about to have his Hoothoot stop the clock, Hoothoot starts to get confused. The other participants then realize that his business is fake. His cover blown, the Bird Keeper quickly retreats.

[[File:Bird Keeper F Adventures.png|thumb|200px|A female Bird Keeper in Pokémon Adventures]]
The same Bird Keeper reappears in ''[[PS137|Really Raikou & Entirely Entei (Part 1)]]'', where he encounters [[Falkner]], as he too specializes in bird Pokémon. He shows Falkner his collection of recently caught Pokémon, much to the {{ci|Violet}} [[Gym Leader]]'s interest. The Bird Keeper does not give any of them away. When {{p|Raikou}} and {{p|Entei}} appear, the Bird Keeper gets excited and wants to catch them. Entei almost attacks him, but Falkner, flying on his {{p|Skarmory}}, grabs him just before he is hit. He is then seen riding on Falkner's Skarmory while Falkner battles the two legendary Pokémon. The Bird Keeper has trouble keeping up with Skarmory's flying speed. He continues to ride on Falkner's Skarmory in ''[[PS138|Really Raikou & Entirely Entei (Part 2)]]'', watching Falkner take on the legendary beasts. After Falkner fails to catch them, the Bird Keeper gets trapped by a boomerang Poké Ball and arrested by Falkner.

He makes a cameo in ''[[PS179|The Last Battle XIII]]'' as one of the people who volunteered their Pokémon for transfer.

===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS327|Facing Gulpin Is Hard to Swallow]]'', a virtual Bird Keeper using a {{p|Taillow}} is seen at the {{gdis|Battle Tower|III}}.

===={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}====
A Bird Keeper appears amongst the people visiting the {{safari|Johto}} in ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]''.

===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
A female Bird Keeper makes an appearance as a background character in the ''Platinum chapter''. She first appeared with a crowd entering the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} when [[Palmer]] told his assistants to open the gates. Later, she saw {{adv|Looker}} flying on his jetpack while he was looking for {{adv|Platinum}}.

